  "conclusion": "NO_GOLDILOCKS_SIZE: for every swept size a kernel is either too short to reconcile the dual-source duration OR its NVBit trace exceeds the budget / is not practically traceable; per-cell tri-label is structurally infeasible for the duration leg, motivating an engineering-closure artifact.",
  "interpretation": {
    "production_duration_reconcile_floor_note": "The authoritative dual-source reconcile floor is the committed sm120_duration_cohort.json / duration_admitted.json (the production --shape-point + override path): the smallest reconciling cells are ~n=2048 (flash_attn_fwd lg ~5.9ms, gemm_hmma_bf16 lg ~8.5ms). A single kernel must run >~2-3ms for host enqueue/sync overhead to fall under 5%, i.e. n >~ 1500.",
    "timing_shape_caveat": "The per-point `duration` column uses --timing_shape (this sweep tool's harness); it scales with size but reconciles differently from the production --shape-point + override path used by collect_portable_lcd_duration.py (which DID reconcile the committed cohort cells at n=2048). The decisive, harness-independent result is the TRACE-size ceiling vs the committed-cohort reconcile floor; the duration column is supplementary size-scaling evidence.",
    "trace_admissible_ceiling_note": "MEASURED: the largest swept GEMM size whose NVBit trace is <= the 64 MiB budget is n=512 (~60 MiB, trace_status=measured, byte_budget_status=within_budget). At n=768 the GEMM trace is MEASURED OVER BUDGET (trace_status=measured, byte_budget_status=over_budget, ~120-209 MiB) \u2014 a measured byte fact, NOT a timeout. The attention slugs instead TIME OUT at n=512 (trace_status=timeout, byte size UNMEASURED). So the trace-admissible ceiling is n=512 for GEMM (sub-millisecond); no admissible size exceeds ~512^3, by measured bytes for GEMM and by timeout for attention.",
    "windows_disjoint": true,
    "windows_disjoint_note": "Measured trace-admissible sizes (<= n=512 for GEMM; attention not traceable at 512 within the cap) are all sub-millisecond, far below the >~2-3ms (>=~n=1500-2048) dual-source reconcile floor. At n=768 the GEMM trace is MEASURED over budget (~120-209 MiB); attention at n=512 times out. So no single (slug, size) is both trace-budget-admissible and duration-reconciling -- the windows are disjoint by the MEASURED admissible ceiling vs the reconcile floor (and by measured over-budget bytes for GEMM at n=768)."
  },
